---
// Terms of use for the site and the free consultation and quote, plus the ground rules that sit around every
// written quote: monthly plans and how they cancel (California's automatic renewal law wants
// this spelled out), texts to and from us, and limits of liability.
// Keep it in line with how quotes and billing actually work.
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';

const email = 'beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com';
---

<Doc
  title="Terms of Use"
  kicker="Legal"
  updated="October 22, 2026"
  description="The terms for using futureclaritytechnologies.com, asking for a free quote, and working with FutureClarity Technologies, including texts, monthly plans and how to cancel."
>
  <p>
    These terms cover futureclaritytechnologies.com and working with FutureClarity Technologies ("we",
    "us"). By using the site or asking for a free quote, you agree to them. Our
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle information, including cookies.
  </p>

  <div class="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The consultation and quote are free, with no obligation.</li>
      <li>You get a written quote before any work starts.</li>
      <li>Once you've paid for it, what we build is yours to keep.</li>
      <li>Monthly plans, such as hosting or care, are optional, and you can cancel any time with no fee.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Quotes</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is a price offer. What you pay is set in a written quote, before any work
    starts. If something in a quote or signed agreement differs from these terms, the quote or agreement
    wins.
  </p>

  <h2>The free consultation and quote</h2>
  <p>
    The consultation and quote are free and come with no obligation to buy anything. We may decline or
    reschedule a consultation. Any review of your site or app that we send you is our honest read of
    what we could see at the time, based on public information and automated checks, which can miss
    things. Designs, mockups or demos we show you before you buy are for trying things out, and stay ours
    until you pay for the work.
  </p>

  <h2>Monthly plans and cancelling</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Monthly plans</strong>, such as hosting, care or a pay-monthly website, are optional. If you choose
      one, your quote shows the monthly price, and the plan renews each month until you cancel.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cancel any time</strong> by email to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, a text or call to
      <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>, or the same way you signed up. There's no cancellation
      fee. You won't be charged for any month after the one in which you cancel, and we'll confirm the
      cancellation in writing.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a monthly price is going to change, we'll tell you in writing at least 30 days before, so you can
      cancel first.
    </li>
    <li>
      A pay-monthly website includes hosting and edits while the plan is active. If your quote includes a
      buyout or a minimum term, it says so up front.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Texts from us</h2>
  <p>
    When you ask for a free quote or contact us with your phone number, you agree we may text you about your
    request: setting up your consultation, your quote and your project. Some texts may be sent with automated
    tools. Agreeing isn't a condition of buying anything. How often we text depends on your request.
    Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to stop at any time, or HELP for help, or reach us at
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>. Carriers
    aren't liable for delayed or undelivered messages. Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains
    how we handle your number; we never share it or your consent with anyone for their marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Texts and emails our automations send</h2>
  <p>
    Many of the workflows we build send texts or emails to your customers, such as reminders, review
    requests and missed-call replies. You're responsible for having your customers' permission to contact
    them and for following the laws that apply, such as the Telephone Consumer Protection Act and
    CAN-SPAM. We set these up with opt-outs (customers can reply STOP), and we'll tell you if a workflow
    needs consent you may not have. Texting services may also need your business registered with the
    phone carriers, which we help with. Review requests must go to every customer alike, never only to
    happy ones, and must never offer anything in return for a review, as Google's and the FTC's rules
    require.
  </p>

  <h2>Your accounts and other software</h2>
  <p>
    If you skip a monthly plan, we set things up on your own accounts, and you pay those services' usage
    costs directly. Software from other companies that we connect to, such as booking tools and texting
    services, has its own terms, and we aren't responsible for those services or their outages.
  </p>

  <h2>What's yours</h2>
  <p>
    Once you've paid for it, what we build for you (your site, app or automations) is yours to keep, as your quote
    describes. Your business information stays yours. This website's content and design belong to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    Please don't misuse the site: no attempts to break in, overload it, scrape it, or send us false
    information. The team pages are for our team only. Links to other websites are there for your
    convenience; we don't control those sites.
  </p>

  <h2>No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to get things right, and your quote describes what we'll deliver. Beyond that, the site
    and the free consultation are provided as they are, and we can't promise any particular business result,
    such as more customers, bookings or search rankings.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits on liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect or consequential losses, such as lost
    profits. Our total liability for any claim about the site or a free consultation is limited to $100, and for
    paid work, to what you paid us for that work in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing here limits
    rights you have under law that can't be waived.
  </p>

  <h2>California law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by California law. Any dispute that we can't settle by talking it over will
    be handled in the courts of Los Angeles County, California.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms and will post the new version here with a new date. Changes don't apply to
    work you've already agreed to in a quote.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    FutureClarity Technologies, San Fernando Valley, California ·
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> · <a href="tel:+18189397964">(818) 939-7964</a>
  </p>
</Doc>
